{"journal_version":1,"sequence":9,"replace_from":10,"message_count":11,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":"**Change**\n\n`app/page.tsx`: added the `\"use client\"` directive as the first line, ahead of the `useState` import. The component was being treated as a Server Component (no parent marked client), so its `useState` hooks were invalid. Nothing else in the component changed — markup, class names, handlers, and the `Checkbox`/`Input`/`Button` usage are untouched.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n\n- `git diff app/page.tsx` (read-only, to confirm the exact edit)\n- `verify_frontend` → runs `npm run verify:agent` (`node .harness/render-smoke.mjs`): exit code 0, `render smoke passed: HTTP 200, 558 bytes`\n\n**Remaining risks**\n\n- The render smoke only proves the page renders and returns HTTP 200; it does not exercise interactivity, so add/toggle behavior is verified by inspection rather than by test.\n- Only `app/page.tsx` was marked as a Client Component. If any of the imported UI components (`components/ui/input`, `checkbox`, `button`) themselves use hooks or browser APIs, they would still need their own boundary — I did not inspect them, as the task scoped the fix to the primary source.\n- Not addressed (out of scope, pre-existing): `handleToggleComplete` takes an untyped `index`, and the list uses array index as `key`.","response_items":[{"id":"4674c409-0a15-4465-844b-64cc8ee318df","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"**Change**\n\n`app/page.tsx`: added the `\"use client\"` directive as the first line, ahead of the `useState` import. The component was being treated as a Server Component (no parent marked client), so its `useState` hooks were invalid. Nothing else in the component changed — markup, class names, handlers, and the `Checkbox`/`Input`/`Button` usage are untouched.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n\n- `git diff app/page.tsx` (read-only, to confirm the exact edit)\n- `verify_frontend` → runs `npm run verify:agent` (`node .harness/render-smoke.mjs`): exit code 0, `render smoke passed: HTTP 200, 558 bytes`\n\n**Remaining risks**\n\n- The render smoke only proves the page renders and returns HTTP 200; it does not exercise interactivity, so add/toggle behavior is verified by inspection rather than by test.\n- Only `app/page.tsx` was marked as a Client Component. If any of the imported UI components (`components/ui/input`, `checkbox`, `button`) themselves use hooks or browser APIs, they would still need their own boundary — I did not inspect them, as the task scoped the fix to the primary source.\n- Not addressed (out of scope, pre-existing): `handleToggleComplete` takes an untyped `index`, and the list uses array index as `key`.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-23T05:26:52.023382+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":11357,"context_tokens":2576,"step_count":5,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["acfbe2cdd7049d2db70952173174e3eb","7530c125ab4e13dcbaabd29607f82f78","3c45d71dcb1acaddc13d0e86e5418077","62ee204ab04cbaac847c6386000d8080"],"reads_since_last_edit":0,"has_landed_write":true,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":4,"scout_ledger":[{"tool":"file_read","target":"app/page.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: app/page.tsx (71 lines total, showing 1-71) 1 import { useState } from \"react\"; 2 import { Input } from \"@/components/ui/input\"; 3 import { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\"; 4 import { Checkbox } from \"@/components/ui/checkbox\";"},{"tool":"file_write","target":"app/page.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Replaced in app/page.tsx: 33 chars → 48 chars (content changed)"},{"tool":"verify_frontend","target":"{}","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Exit code: 0 > my-app@0.1.0 verify:agent > node .harness/render-smoke.mjs render smoke passed: HTTP 200, 558 bytes"},{"tool":"git_diff","target":"